16:19.731 --> 16:21.025
- And this one?
- "Kneivel. "

16:21.108 --> 16:22.150
- And this one?
- "Was. "

16:22.235 --> 16:23.360
- And this one?
- "Born. "

16:23.443 --> 16:24.486
- And this one?
- "In. "

16:24.570 --> 16:26.572
- And this one?
- "Montana. "

16:27.032 --> 16:30.369
Hey, Lois. Did you know
that Evel Kneivel was born in Montana?

16:33.915 --> 16:35.209
You didn't tell her?

16:35.335 --> 16:37.044
Look, I told you she was gonna kill herself.

16:37.168 --> 16:38.295
What was I supposed to do?

16:38.420 --> 16:41.550
Let her. No, that's not funny.

16:41.675 --> 16:42.717
Wait a second.

16:42.801 --> 16:44.887
We know she's gonna be upset
if you dump her.

16:44.971 --> 16:47.224
But if something happened that
was out of your control...

16:47.308 --> 16:50.395
- What do you mean?
- I mean we're gonna fake your death.

16:50.519 --> 16:53.856
This is the best idea
I've had since I invented that soda.

16:53.940 --> 16:56.735
Gentlemen, I give you Crystal Pepsi.

16:56.818 --> 17:00.489
All the great taste of regular Pepsi
but without the troublesome opacity.

17:00.614 --> 17:02.451
Well, what if you're drinking
a regular Pepsi

17:02.575 --> 17:04.368
and somebody is coming at you
with a knife, huh?

17:04.453 --> 17:06.330
You won't be able to see him
past your Pepsi.

17:06.455 --> 17:08.832
And then, who's dead, huh? You.

17:08.958 --> 17:10.753
You! You're dead! Stabbed!

17:10.837 --> 17:12.130
Crystal Pepsi.

17:15.925 --> 17:17.593
All right, fellas. I think we did it.

17:17.719 --> 17:20.931
This may be
the most absolutely perfect fake death

17:21.056 --> 17:23.269
in the history of fake deaths.

17:24.520 --> 17:25.771
What do you guys want?

17:25.895 --> 17:28.275
Joan, um, you mind if we come in?

17:28.525 --> 17:31.195
There's, um... There's been an accident.

17:31.819 --> 17:34.281
This is, uh, not gonna be easy,

17:34.365 --> 17:36.784
but it's something you should see.

17:38.494 --> 17:40.790
So, anyway, here's Quagmire
walking through the park,

17:40.915 --> 17:42.250
minding his own business.

17:42.334 --> 17:44.877
I just happened to be there
with my video camera

17:45.002 --> 17:46.838
when a ninja shows up!

17:48.048 --> 17:49.801
And then a Nazi came!

17:51.260 --> 17:53.806
And then an evil pots-and-pans robot!

17:54.140 --> 17:55.558
Destroy.

17:55.683 --> 17:56.893
Destroy.

17:57.561 --> 18:00.313
I imagine you're probably wondering
what happened to the body.

18:00.439 --> 18:02.150
Well, we thought of that.

18:02.233 --> 18:04.777
Oh, no! Quagmire's dead!

18:04.861 --> 18:08.073
Wait! We might still be able to save...
Oh, no!

18:19.880 --> 18:22.842
We are so, so sorry for your loss.

18:22.926 --> 18:24.220
Is this a joke?

18:24.344 --> 18:27.222
I wish it were, Joan. I wish it were a joke.

18:27.306 --> 18:29.475
But these things happen, you know?

18:29.558 --> 18:31.352
You go for a walk in the park one day,

18:31.435 --> 18:35.023
and wheelchair ninjas, and Nazis, and
pots-and-pans robots show up to kill you,

18:35.149 --> 18:37.652
and dinosaurs show up to eat the remains.
You've seen the news.

18:37.735 --> 18:39.278
You're not fooling anyone.

18:39.403 --> 18:41.071
All right, fellows. Plan B.

18:41.197 --> 18:42.282
Plan B, Quagmire.

18:42.407 --> 18:44.034
Hi, honey. I'm home.

18:44.118 --> 18:45.703
Heart attack!

18:47.748 --> 18:50.920
Glenn, sweetheart! Is he all right?

18:51.044 --> 18:53.503
No, he's dead. I can tell. I'm a cop.

18:53.587 --> 18:55.758
Oh, my God! Are you sure?

18:55.883 --> 18:59.929
You know what'll prove it?
When people die, they void their bowels.

19:00.055 --> 19:03.769
I said, when people die,
they void their bowels.

19:04.603 --> 19:06.437
Oh, my God!

19:07.229 --> 19:08.732
What a jackass.

19:12.319 --> 19:14.573
- Well, you look a lot better.
- I did it, Brian!

19:14.657 --> 19:16.075
Through sheer force of will,

19:16.159 --> 19:17.828
I kicked my addiction to breast milk.

19:17.953 --> 19:20.663
I just had to find a way
to make breasts seem repulsive.

19:20.789 --> 19:23.417
<i>- Yeah. How did you do that?
- I watched In The Cut.</i>

19:23.501 --> 19:26.755
Meg Ryan topless. No, thanks. No, thanks.

19:27.005 --> 19:30.134
Stewie, Mommy has a surprise for you.

19:30.260 --> 19:31.427
What are you doing?

19:31.511 --> 19:33.512
Oh, Brian, I thought
I was ready to wean him.

19:33.637 --> 19:35.765
But I just miss the bonding.

19:35.849 --> 19:39.353
No, no! No, put me down! I beg of you!

19:39.479 --> 19:41.856
I just kicked the stuff. Damn you!

19:42.567 --> 19:44.277
You sick, twisted...

19:44.485 --> 19:45.778
I hate you.

19:46.027 --> 19:47.363
I love it.

19:47.864 --> 19:49.448
I will kill you.

19:56.082 --> 19:58.294
You sure Quagmire's okay in there?

19:58.378 --> 20:00.629
No problem.
He's got half an hour of oxygen.

20:00.713 --> 20:03.341
We'll sneak back later and dig him up.

20:04.885 --> 20:08.222
<i>Sorry, I'm late.
I had a meeting over at NBC about Joey.</i>

20:08.347 --> 20:11.185
Death? What are you doing here?
Nobody's dying today.

20:11.310 --> 20:12.936
Not according to my paperwork.

20:13.020 --> 20:15.523
Says here your buddy Quagmire
died of a heart attack.

20:15.648 --> 20:18.944
I got to tell you,
I always thought it would be rectal trauma.

20:21.864 --> 20:23.491
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
What the hell are you doing?

20:23.575 --> 20:25.328
Well, Mayor West is afraid of zombies.

20:25.411 --> 20:28.538
So the city says
all caskets must be encased in concrete.

20:28.664 --> 20:31.543
You'll thank me
when no one eats our brains.

20:31.627 --> 20:32.837
You'll thank me.

20:32.962 --> 20:36.383
Hold it! Stop the funeral.
Quagmire's not really dead.

20:38.720 --> 20:39.843
Zombie!

20:43.350 --> 20:45.810
Glenn, I thought I'd lost you.

20:45.894 --> 20:49.566
Sorry, Mr. Quagmire, but I still need a body
to take back with me.

20:49.692 --> 20:52.360
- So...
- No, you can't take him.

20:56.448 --> 20:59.995
You know, this is probably not cool.
Just throwing it out there.

21:00.078 --> 21:02.582
- She was suicidal.
- She was?

21:02.665 --> 21:04.626
- Yeah, absolutely.
- I had heard that, too.

21:04.750 --> 21:06.294
And her last name was Quagmire.

21:06.418 --> 21:07.546
Well, good enough for me.

21:07.629 --> 21:10.092
I got to go. I got tickets to Celine Dion.

21:10.216 --> 21:13.637
I'm not gonna kill her,
I'm just gonna watch her die on her own.

21:13.762 --> 21:15.222
Anyone? Anyone?

21:16.432 --> 21:18.559
Ah, it's good to have you back, Quagmire.

21:18.643 --> 21:20.771
It's good to be back, Peter.

21:21.104 --> 21:24.525
Hey, Death, can you leave
that body here for another five minutes?

21:26.194 --> 21:27.571
That's Quagmire.

21:27.572 --> 22:28.572
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru